1
00:00:03,056 --> 00:00:04,391
It's finally here.

2
00:00:04,474 --> 00:00:05,976
Ishiai Koji's cat book!

3
00:00:06,059 --> 00:00:08,562
I love that Mom sends
pictures of Momohiki,

4
00:00:08,645 --> 00:00:10,814
but this is an extra cat boost for my day.

5
00:00:10,897 --> 00:00:13,358
Let the healing begin!

6
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:17,487
Huh? Has it already been a month
since Kazuki moved in?

7
00:00:18,071 --> 00:00:20,824
Guess he'll be finding a new place soon.

8
00:00:21,575 --> 00:00:24,911
Living with Junta and Kazuki
has been surprisingly fun.

9
00:00:24,995 --> 00:00:27,205
It'll be strange when he moves out.

10
00:00:27,748 --> 00:00:28,790
ARISA: CAN WE MEET?

11
00:00:28,874 --> 00:00:31,334
Speaking of strange, I wonder
who that text was from--

12
00:00:31,418 --> 00:00:32,878
I know, right?

13
00:00:34,087 --> 00:00:35,130
My book!

14
00:00:38,341 --> 00:00:40,135
What the hell do you think you're doing?

15
00:00:40,218 --> 00:00:42,721
I was just waiting
for the light to change.

16
00:00:43,305 --> 00:00:46,141
He bumped into me.
I should be the one yelling.

17
00:00:46,224 --> 00:00:49,019
It's all thanks to you
that I dropped my coffee.

18
00:00:49,102 --> 00:00:50,854
And ruined my shoes.

19
00:00:50,937 --> 00:00:52,856
-You're gonna pay for that!
-Hey!

20
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:54,983
-Uh…
-That's enough.

21
00:00:56,276 --> 00:00:57,110
Huh?

22
00:00:58,195 --> 00:01:00,113
You're the one who bumped into her.

23
00:01:02,407 --> 00:01:05,327
Ah, dude. You're, like, crazy hot.

24
00:01:05,410 --> 00:01:08,830
What do you say, you pay back
your little friend's debt with a date?

25
00:01:13,502 --> 00:01:15,670
-Don't ever touch me.
-Ow…

26
00:01:15,754 --> 00:01:17,339
Now apologize to her.

27
00:01:17,923 --> 00:01:19,841
It's just a stupid book!

28
00:01:19,925 --> 00:01:21,802
Just a book?

29
00:01:22,427 --> 00:01:25,555
You have no idea what I've lost!

30
00:01:25,639 --> 00:01:27,849
This book is worth
hours of healing!

31
00:01:29,017 --> 00:01:32,020
I curse you!
May stray cats infest your house

32
00:01:32,104 --> 00:01:33,939
and soak your bed in cat pee!

33
00:01:34,022 --> 00:01:36,191
You're gonna drill straight into my brain!

34
00:01:38,026 --> 00:01:39,569
I'm sorry!

35
00:01:40,237 --> 00:01:41,947
-Ow!
-Uh…

36
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:45,242
My head… the pain.
That chick's crazy.

37
00:01:47,786 --> 00:01:50,956
Maybe next time
you'll be a little bit more respectful.

38
00:01:54,709 --> 00:01:56,545
Let's go.

39
00:01:56,628 --> 00:01:59,172
Your book okay? Sorry about those jerks.

40
00:01:59,256 --> 00:02:01,007
Heh?

41
00:02:04,094 --> 00:02:07,264
Oh yeah, the book's fine.
Thanks for saving me.

42
00:02:07,347 --> 00:02:09,057
Oh my gosh, she'll think I'm in love!

43
00:02:09,141 --> 00:02:12,018
I hope I don't look as dumb
as I feel right now!

44
00:02:13,019 --> 00:02:14,479
Did you really

45
00:02:14,563 --> 00:02:16,773
curse him with a cat-pee-soaked mattress?

46
00:02:16,857 --> 00:02:20,026
It was all I could think of.
You can never get that smell out.

47
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:21,236
-Arisa.
-Huh?

48
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,113
Hey, Tsukasa.

49
00:02:23,196 --> 00:02:24,364
Kazuki?

50
00:02:24,447 --> 00:02:26,533
Hoshino? You know each other?

51
00:02:26,616 --> 00:02:27,826
Hoshino, like…

52
00:02:28,493 --> 00:02:30,662
Wait, are you Anzu Hoshino?

53
00:02:30,745 --> 00:02:31,830
Me? Um…

54
00:02:32,789 --> 00:02:34,833
I'm Arisa, Tsukasa's big sister.

55
00:02:34,916 --> 00:02:36,543
Thanks for looking after him.

56
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:42,048
Uh, legendary good looks
run in your family.

57
00:02:42,132 --> 00:02:44,593
So bright, can't look directly at it!

58
00:02:44,676 --> 00:02:45,677
You're an idiot.

59
00:04:17,143 --> 00:04:19,187
#8 THE PHOENIX RISES! I AM A BIRD!

60
00:04:19,271 --> 00:04:23,108
Thanks for having me. Are you sure
that I'm not barging in here?

61
00:04:23,191 --> 00:04:24,276
Of course not.

62
00:04:24,818 --> 00:04:27,320
Thanks again
for letting Tsukasa stay here.

63
00:04:27,404 --> 00:04:29,239
A month is a long time.

64
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:30,907
No, not at all.

65
00:04:30,991 --> 00:04:33,827
Really, it's been awesome
having him around.

66
00:04:33,910 --> 00:04:36,579
Not to mention
this whole thing is my fault.

67
00:04:37,747 --> 00:04:40,917
My mother and I
should have introduced ourselves sooner.

68
00:04:41,418 --> 00:04:43,378
To be honest, we were a bit surprised.

69
00:04:43,461 --> 00:04:45,505
We didn't think he'd be staying this long.

70
00:04:45,588 --> 00:04:48,967
Between the pipe bursting
and the new phone, it's been chaotic.

71
00:04:49,050 --> 00:04:51,303
So I figured it was probably
best for me to come out

72
00:04:51,386 --> 00:04:52,971
and get the details in person.

73
00:04:53,596 --> 00:04:55,682
Oh yeah, that makes sense.

74
00:04:56,182 --> 00:04:59,602
The phone…
Yeah, that was my fault too.

75
00:04:59,686 --> 00:05:03,189
Oh. Hey, would you like
something to drink?

76
00:05:03,273 --> 00:05:06,234
I think we have some iced tea, or, um…

77
00:05:06,318 --> 00:05:08,820
-Uh, there's a fresh pitcher.
-Oh, that would be great.

78
00:05:10,947 --> 00:05:13,950
Better let Mom know everything's okay.

79
00:05:15,452 --> 00:05:18,371
So, did something happen
at the station? You looked frazzled.

80
00:05:18,455 --> 00:05:23,335
Oh. This guy bumped into me,
then tried to pick a fight with me.

81
00:05:23,418 --> 00:05:24,252
What?

82
00:05:25,337 --> 00:05:27,964
But your sister totally saved me.

83
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,675
Those guys didn't stand a chance.

84
00:05:30,759 --> 00:05:32,927
You know what? Your sister's really cool.

85
00:05:33,011 --> 00:05:35,096
Yeah, but she had a tendency
to find trouble.

86
00:05:36,598 --> 00:05:37,557
I'm sorry that happened.

87
00:05:38,058 --> 00:05:39,184
Nah, it's fine,

88
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:42,979
'cause I cursed him with a mattress
completely soaked in cat pee!

89
00:05:43,063 --> 00:05:46,608
So yeah, it's all good.

90
00:05:46,691 --> 00:05:51,029
Seriously?
A mattress soaked in cat pee?

91
00:05:51,112 --> 00:05:53,239
No, it really is the worst!

92
00:05:57,410 --> 00:05:58,745
Sorry to keep you waiting.

93
00:05:58,828 --> 00:06:00,580
All good, thanks.

94
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:05,126
Kazuki, I'm just curious.

95
00:06:05,210 --> 00:06:07,337
Why did you wanna go to our school
and live alone?

96
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:12,550
Uh, you don't have to answer that.
I shouldn't have asked.

97
00:06:12,634 --> 00:06:16,012
Hmm… Well, how do I say this?

98
00:06:19,849 --> 00:06:22,018
Huh?

99
00:06:22,602 --> 00:06:24,729
Our father's a real piece of garbage.

100
00:06:24,813 --> 00:06:25,647
SHIT

101
00:06:25,730 --> 00:06:27,524
Piece of garbage?

102
00:06:28,108 --> 00:06:30,193
Yup. That's why our mom decided

103
00:06:30,276 --> 00:06:32,362
it was best for Tsukasa
to go to school out here.

104
00:06:32,445 --> 00:06:33,279
Oh.

105
00:06:34,656 --> 00:06:36,449
I'm not wrong, am I?

106
00:06:36,533 --> 00:06:37,534
No.

107
00:06:39,994 --> 00:06:42,789
I was really worried
when I heard you'd be living alone.

108
00:06:43,623 --> 00:06:46,709
I'm relieved you're staying
with someone sweet like Anzu.

109
00:06:50,255 --> 00:06:51,297
Oh, Makoto.

110
00:06:52,715 --> 00:06:54,426
Um, hey.

111
00:06:54,509 --> 00:06:55,427
What's up?

112
00:06:57,804 --> 00:07:00,640
-Who's Makoto?
-He's a friend from school.

113
00:07:01,307 --> 00:07:02,308
Oh.

114
00:07:02,809 --> 00:07:05,311
Hey, what's Tsukasa like
at school, anyway?

115
00:07:05,812 --> 00:07:09,691
Well, uh, he's popular
but keeps to himself.

116
00:07:11,151 --> 00:07:13,611
Being reserved makes everyone
like him even more.

117
00:07:13,695 --> 00:07:14,863
And you?

118
00:07:15,488 --> 00:07:17,782
You seem to like him too, huh?

119
00:07:19,701 --> 00:07:20,535
Huh?

120
00:07:20,618 --> 00:07:21,536
It's not like that.

121
00:07:21,619 --> 00:07:23,705
I swear on my unborn descendants.

122
00:07:23,788 --> 00:07:24,914
That's a bit extreme.

123
00:07:25,457 --> 00:07:28,626
In fact, I didn't like him
when I first met him.

124
00:07:29,961 --> 00:07:31,129
But…

125
00:07:31,212 --> 00:07:33,423
I'm glad I took the time
to get to know him better.

126
00:07:34,132 --> 00:07:36,718
'Cause, you know,
now he's a really great friend.

127
00:07:39,971 --> 00:07:43,266
You know, he used to be
a really social kid.

128
00:07:43,349 --> 00:07:46,227
He was always smiling,
befriending everyone he met.

129
00:07:47,061 --> 00:07:48,730
I can't picture that.

130
00:07:48,813 --> 00:07:50,315
I know, right?

131
00:07:51,316 --> 00:07:54,611
There was a problem
back when he was in junior high.

132
00:07:54,694 --> 00:07:57,363
Ever since then, he sort of shut down.

133
00:07:57,447 --> 00:08:01,534
So before, the way he was laughing
with you, I haven't seen that side

134
00:08:01,618 --> 00:08:04,370
of my little brother
in a really long time.

135
00:08:05,038 --> 00:08:05,914
Huh?

136
00:08:06,456 --> 00:08:08,541
You bring it out of him, Anzu.

137
00:08:09,125 --> 00:08:10,668
Really, it's not--

138
00:08:10,752 --> 00:08:11,878
Huh?

139
00:08:11,961 --> 00:08:13,880
He wanted me to go to a movie,

140
00:08:14,422 --> 00:08:16,883
but I think he really just wanted
someone to vent to.

141
00:08:17,759 --> 00:08:19,677
-About what?
-Oh…

142
00:08:20,386 --> 00:08:22,430
Something about his sister
stealing his last pudding.

143
00:08:22,514 --> 00:08:23,389
MAKOTO
IT WAS DELICIOUS

144
00:08:24,390 --> 00:08:25,517
Tell him next time

145
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,060
to write his name on it.

146
00:08:27,143 --> 00:08:28,645
He did. She ate it anyway.

147
00:08:29,354 --> 00:08:33,191
Hmm. There's no stronger grudge
than one held over food.

148
00:08:33,274 --> 00:08:34,526
Is it that big a deal?

149
00:08:35,109 --> 00:08:36,736
I don't make the rules.

150
00:08:44,619 --> 00:08:46,120
About your friend, Anzu.

151
00:08:47,121 --> 00:08:49,415
She's sweet. I'm just surprised
you're friends with her.

152
00:08:50,416 --> 00:08:53,044
I thought
you were still avoiding all girls.

153
00:08:56,839 --> 00:08:59,634
Yeah, I know. I wasn't planning on it.

154
00:09:00,635 --> 00:09:03,805
But she's different.
I feel more at ease with her.

155
00:09:04,472 --> 00:09:07,392
Tsukasa, why don't you just
stay here a while?

156
00:09:07,892 --> 00:09:09,102
Huh?

157
00:09:09,185 --> 00:09:10,603
Calm down, it's a joke.

158
00:09:11,312 --> 00:09:13,064
Uh… uh…

159
00:09:14,232 --> 00:09:15,817
Uh, well…

160
00:09:16,359 --> 00:09:18,778
I don't mind if you don't mind.

161
00:09:18,861 --> 00:09:19,988
Hm?

162
00:09:21,197 --> 00:09:23,157
You've been so helpful around here.

163
00:09:23,241 --> 00:09:25,910
And maybe it's just me,
but I think it's been a lot of fun

164
00:09:25,994 --> 00:09:27,036
living with you and Junta.

165
00:09:27,787 --> 00:09:31,040
Not to mention Riri's scheming
if you leave Junta and I alone.

166
00:09:31,124 --> 00:09:32,333
Most importantly,

167
00:09:32,417 --> 00:09:35,712
you're the only one brave enough
to kill all those bugs!

168
00:09:37,130 --> 00:09:39,090
If it's that important to you,

169
00:09:39,882 --> 00:09:41,342
then I guess I'll stay.

170
00:09:43,636 --> 00:09:44,637
Hm.

171
00:09:45,388 --> 00:09:48,558
Yeah? This will be great!

172
00:09:48,641 --> 00:09:50,393
There's another show
I've been dying to watch.

173
00:09:50,476 --> 00:09:51,311
Sure.

174
00:09:51,978 --> 00:09:55,523
I get it now. That's why
you never wanted to talk about her.

175
00:09:56,899 --> 00:09:59,277
You were embarrassed I'd figure it out.

176
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,820
That she makes you smile again.

177
00:10:02,322 --> 00:10:03,197
Um…

178
00:10:05,116 --> 00:10:07,201
-Wait, do you like--
-It's not like that.

179
00:10:08,328 --> 00:10:10,288
With Hoshino, I can be myself.

180
00:10:10,788 --> 00:10:13,124
For me, that's all I need.

181
00:10:18,046 --> 00:10:19,047
Okay.

182
00:10:25,219 --> 00:10:27,597
I'm glad
I met Kazuki's sister today.

183
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:29,974
I learned a lot more about him.

184
00:10:32,018 --> 00:10:33,353
Hey, you're back.

185
00:10:34,896 --> 00:10:37,148
You have the coolest sister.

186
00:10:37,231 --> 00:10:39,692
I loved getting to meet her.

187
00:10:39,776 --> 00:10:42,403
I should have worn something nicer.
This outfit sucks.

188
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,949
I really assumed you thought
that outfit was appropriate

189
00:10:47,033 --> 00:10:47,950
to meet guests.

190
00:10:48,034 --> 00:10:49,285
No way.

191
00:10:49,369 --> 00:10:51,704
I learned a lot
when we went shopping together.

192
00:10:51,788 --> 00:10:54,457
I've tried to be more mindful
about what I wear since then.

193
00:10:55,667 --> 00:10:58,419
Man, I wish I had
a big sister like her.

194
00:11:00,088 --> 00:11:01,005
Hoshino.

195
00:11:01,506 --> 00:11:03,800
What Arisa said
about why I lived by myself…

196
00:11:05,885 --> 00:11:06,803
Yeah?

197
00:11:07,470 --> 00:11:08,513
Uh, uh--

198
00:11:10,932 --> 00:11:13,518
Never mind. Maybe another day.

199
00:11:15,228 --> 00:11:16,396
Hmm…

200
00:11:17,271 --> 00:11:19,232
Uh, okay.

201
00:11:22,735 --> 00:11:24,487
Is it just me or…

202
00:11:25,571 --> 00:11:27,573
Is this warm feeling friendship?

203
00:11:27,657 --> 00:11:30,660
Or is this excitement? Love!

204
00:11:31,244 --> 00:11:34,414
Yay! Great job, Anzu, I'm so proud of you!

205
00:11:34,497 --> 00:11:36,791
You were able to get
his big sister's approval,

206
00:11:36,874 --> 00:11:38,459
even just like that.

207
00:11:38,543 --> 00:11:40,795
I tell you how can you find love,
it's so fulfilling.

208
00:11:40,878 --> 00:11:45,675
-Now, let's keep this up--
-You know what? I didn't miss you one bit!

209
00:11:47,468 --> 00:11:50,179
Come on!

210
00:11:50,263 --> 00:11:51,764
A FEW DAYS LATER

211
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:55,435
In order to address low birth rate issues,

212
00:11:57,186 --> 00:12:01,441
Anzu was gifted a real-life dating sim
called Romantic Thriller.

213
00:12:01,524 --> 00:12:03,943
And after many perfect scenarios,

214
00:12:04,026 --> 00:12:08,614
I am reporting that there has been
zero romantic development.

215
00:12:08,698 --> 00:12:10,950
I can't turn this in!

216
00:12:14,537 --> 00:12:17,457
Clearly, I have a lot more research to do.

217
00:12:18,082 --> 00:12:19,917
I have an excellent idea!

218
00:12:20,001 --> 00:12:21,961
-We can go on a date.
-What?

219
00:12:22,712 --> 00:12:25,631
I need to experience
what a real-life date is like,

220
00:12:25,715 --> 00:12:27,467
so you and I will go on a mock date.

221
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:28,968
A mock date?

222
00:12:29,051 --> 00:12:31,304
What are you even talking about?

223
00:12:32,054 --> 00:12:34,056
I'm so over your nonsense.

224
00:12:34,557 --> 00:12:37,935
Aw, don't be such a meanie!

225
00:12:38,019 --> 00:12:38,978
Ha!

226
00:12:39,061 --> 00:12:42,482
-Huh?
-What if I look like this instead?

227
00:12:43,483 --> 00:12:45,485
Wait!
There's a boy version of you too?

228
00:12:47,111 --> 00:12:49,739
Whatever. Doesn't change anything.

229
00:12:50,323 --> 00:12:52,241
I'm not asking you to do this for free.

230
00:12:52,325 --> 00:12:54,243
-Huh?
-I'll buy you those cat pajamas

231
00:12:54,327 --> 00:12:56,829
you saw in the mall.
The one with the hoodies and tail.

232
00:12:58,164 --> 00:12:59,290
It's a deal.

233
00:12:59,373 --> 00:13:00,833
Let go!

234
00:13:01,584 --> 00:13:04,921
Whoo! Can't believe I'm on my first date!

235
00:13:05,004 --> 00:13:06,214
Tell me…

236
00:13:08,883 --> 00:13:10,718
Why did I have to dress up for this?

237
00:13:10,802 --> 00:13:12,345
It's a date.

238
00:13:12,428 --> 00:13:14,597
We're not hanging out
at a rest stop for truckers.

239
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,933
Hey! Do I really dress that badly?

240
00:13:17,016 --> 00:13:18,476
Yep, just the worst.

241
00:13:19,310 --> 00:13:20,978
Now, on with our date!

242
00:13:21,062 --> 00:13:21,979
Ugh!

243
00:13:22,563 --> 00:13:25,650
Easy there, I'm not some sort of pervert.

244
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,486
Holding hands is what you do on dates.

245
00:13:28,569 --> 00:13:31,322
I don't care. I don't want people
getting the wrong idea about us.

246
00:13:31,823 --> 00:13:33,991
Hmm…

247
00:13:34,575 --> 00:13:36,536
I'll buy you another cat shirt!

248
00:13:39,705 --> 00:13:41,499
-Fine, then hold my hand.
-Ow, ow, ouch!

249
00:13:42,291 --> 00:13:43,584
So, where are we going?

250
00:13:45,211 --> 00:13:47,672
The most classic of dating activities.
The movies.

251
00:13:49,423 --> 00:13:53,719
A romantic movie always
gets the couple in the mood for love.

252
00:13:53,803 --> 00:13:55,721
Slowly their hands touch.

253
00:13:56,305 --> 00:13:57,306
Huh?

254
00:13:58,307 --> 00:14:00,726
And then, their lips touch.

255
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:03,521
You're twisted.

256
00:14:08,818 --> 00:14:10,903
Is there anything good out right now?

257
00:14:11,487 --> 00:14:13,573
Oh, any cat movies?

258
00:14:13,656 --> 00:14:15,116
No cats! We're on a date,

259
00:14:15,199 --> 00:14:16,576
so we're definitely watching
a romantic movie!

260
00:14:16,659 --> 00:14:17,910
ETERNAL STAR

261
00:14:18,494 --> 00:14:21,289
What? That looks so lame.

262
00:14:21,372 --> 00:14:24,250
One of those tearjerkers
where the girl dies in the end.

263
00:14:24,333 --> 00:14:25,668
Tearjerkers are great!

264
00:14:25,751 --> 00:14:29,005
So much romance,
it'll be the perfect reference material!

265
00:14:29,505 --> 00:14:31,924
Using this kind of movie
is a reference…

266
00:14:32,675 --> 00:14:34,093
doesn't bode well for me.

267
00:14:37,513 --> 00:14:38,806
That was so good!

268
00:14:39,390 --> 00:14:40,933
We've got to do this more often.

269
00:14:41,017 --> 00:14:42,935
-Yeah.
-Hey, look!

270
00:14:43,019 --> 00:14:44,770
-Need the bathroom first.
-Hosshi!

271
00:14:44,854 --> 00:14:46,272
-Huh?
-Hey, you!

272
00:14:46,355 --> 00:14:48,441
Looking good all dressed up.

273
00:14:49,025 --> 00:14:50,693
Kazuki, Makoto.

274
00:14:51,819 --> 00:14:52,778
-Huh?
-Uh?

275
00:14:54,030 --> 00:14:55,948
Oh crap!

276
00:14:56,032 --> 00:14:57,325
How's it going?

277
00:14:57,408 --> 00:15:00,369
I'm Anzu's cousin, Rio. Rio Fushigi.

278
00:15:00,453 --> 00:15:01,913
I'm Riri's twin brother.

279
00:15:01,996 --> 00:15:03,706
Yeah, nice backstory.

280
00:15:03,789 --> 00:15:05,875
This is just great.
All the people in this town

281
00:15:05,958 --> 00:15:07,710
and we had to run into these two?

282
00:15:07,793 --> 00:15:09,545
Wait, didn't he set this up?

283
00:15:09,629 --> 00:15:12,298
All right, we better get going then.
We're on a date.

284
00:15:12,381 --> 00:15:14,216
Hey, don't say stuff like that.

285
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:17,136
Ignore him.
Rio just likes to mess around sometimes.

286
00:15:17,219 --> 00:15:18,054
Bye!

287
00:15:18,554 --> 00:15:21,474
See ya, Hosshi. Oh, and Hosshi's cousin.

288
00:15:22,058 --> 00:15:24,977
They seem oddly close
for being cousins, don't you think?

289
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:30,191
What's your problem?

290
00:15:30,274 --> 00:15:32,026
Calm down, it's a mock date.

291
00:15:32,109 --> 00:15:33,694
Gotta treat it like the real thing.

292
00:15:33,778 --> 00:15:35,905
You're gonna give them
the wrong idea about me.

293
00:15:35,988 --> 00:15:38,074
I'll sue you for defamation!

294
00:15:38,157 --> 00:15:40,451
The lady doth protest too much.

295
00:15:41,035 --> 00:15:44,622
Strange. Usually, he'd get Kazuki
and the others involved

296
00:15:44,705 --> 00:15:46,958
in some crazy dating scenarios.

297
00:15:47,041 --> 00:15:50,127
Maybe he really is trying
to learn about dating.

298
00:15:50,211 --> 00:15:51,212
Too bad for him,

299
00:15:51,295 --> 00:15:54,465
whatever he learns here,
I'll just destroy it!

300
00:15:55,758 --> 00:15:57,426
What's with that face?

301
00:15:57,510 --> 00:16:00,471
Smiling weird like that makes you look
like you're coming unhinged.

302
00:16:01,514 --> 00:16:03,474
There's nothing better than popcorn

